+# Signal runtime integration — design/audit
+Baseline `2bbef42cad5d35a569ab1744f39e31770d56b7f0`. Local/remote matched and worktree was clean at resume. Preserved closure-preflight JAR `9e90a695dfa14ab193849335cb28dffa0d27cb8d212cc87387e260b0f8cb637e` / source `9b77d81bea39c4cea7673fa604e6f8d0af9e6852943ff3772e2d9567fdef1f17` in `evidence/return-network-signal/baseline`.
+
+## Semantic contract
+Checkpoint numbers/facts/transaction/schema remain unchanged. Runtime integration changes WHEN observation can be committed: cp3 requires complete old-pattern playback plus explicit equipment interaction; cp5 requires complete response playback plus explicit equipment interaction. Emission alone no longer implies player observation. This is an intentional player-interaction gate, not a new durable fact. Old saved cp3/5/6 remain accepted; no retroactive replay requirement.
+
+ReturnNetworkPlayback delegates canonical pulse order to existing Support ReturnNetworkSignal. Runtime:10tick lead-in,12tick SHORT,16gap,12SHORT,16gap,36LONG. At nominal20TPS:0.5s lead,0.6s/0.8s/0.6s/0.8s/1.8s. Tuning is not narrative canon; low TPS stretches wall time. Every server Post tick drives playback, independently of10tick NPC navigation. Missed/duplicate tick, readiness loss or carrier rejection cancels the entire transient session. Next start uses a new UUID and complete pattern. Nothing is serialized.
+
+Carrier: vanilla ELECTRIC_SPARK above original relay, every active tick;24 particles with bounded spread. Minecraft1.21.1 GlowParticle.ElectricSparkProvider verified locally: lifetime2-3ticks, well below16tick gap. Quiet note-block bell at volume0.12/pitch1.5 every4active ticks. No persistent LIT toggle, block writes, camera movement, force load, teleport, new entity/reward/monster or audio framework. The existing explicit intervention setBlock remains unchanged.
+
+Participant: exact canonical NPC, same dimension, arrived at STAND; original session observer alive/non-spectator/within6blocks; environmentReady. Confirmation additionally uses existing5block interaction reach and same observer UUID. Signal packets are technical delivery attempts, NOT claims about human perception. The new neutral completion prompt invites inspection without spelling out pattern order. Existing evidence text remains after confirmed observation.
+
+Completed event stays quiet; no automatic ambient replay implemented. cp5+ receipts are never generated by the playback driver. Existing commitReturnNetwork handles all durable commits and readback/hash publication unchanged. Current save5/Actor1/ReturnNetwork1 remain. No Scenario/Audio/Fear framework, transaction subsystem, art work, release promotion or Caveman.
+
+## Test contract
+Six new GameTests cover exact durations/gaps/edges, skipped tick, readiness interruption at multiple boundaries, new-session restart, carrier failure, quiet completed session. Existing102 tests retained. Standalone Support signal27 and load53 rerun separately. Opt-in ReturnNetworkSignalSmoke emits diagnostics, intentional hard exits, screenshot evidence and a40tick no-confirmation hold atcp2 andcp4. The fixture camera aims at the relay only to record screenshots; this is NOT production camera behavior or unaided exploration evidence.
+
+Hard exits on Windows may return native -1073740791 even after the intentional boundary Runtime.halt(0). Cut tasks alone accept0 or that observed abrupt-exit code, and only with exact PASS boundary, matching durable NBT, no-flush marker, PID termination and successful fresh-process recovery. Normal clients must exit0. First CutBefore runner failure is retained, not rewritten as a normal zero exit.
+
+## Failure surfaces still distinct
+Actual renderer frames show light present/absent and spatial anchoring. Server boundary logs prove12/12/36tick emissions and16tick gaps. These do not, by themselves, prove unaided player comprehension or audible quality. All clients remain muted on right secondary DISPLAY1. Final seal requires a separate scene-readability decision, not merely an increased PASS count.
